  "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
  "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDomainPolicy",
  "schema:name": "TrustDomainPolicy",
  "dcterms:title": "GDHCN Trust Domain policy (VC termsOfUse entry)",
  "dcterms:description": "One entry of a W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 `termsOfUse` (section 5.5) naming a policy of a GDHCN Trust Domain that the credential's issuer acts under. One example is a VHL Receiver's self-issued credential under the Verifiable Credential Option of IHE ITI VHL ITI-YY5.\n\nVC 2.0 requires each `termsOfUse` value to have a `type` and allows an `id`. The `type` is this logical model's canonical URL. The `id` is the policy: a code in a Trust Domain's terms-of-use ValueSet, written as `{CodeSystem canonical}#{code}`. A verifier finds the Trust Domain from the ValueSet that holds the policy.\n\n```json\n\"termsOfUse\": [{\n  \"type\": \"http://smart.who.int/trust/StructureDefinition/TrustDomainPolicy\",\n  \"id\": \"http://smart.who.int/ips-pilgrimage/CodeSystem/IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT#CONSENT-KSA\"\n}]\n```",
  "schema:version": "1.7.5",
  "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
